{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_35db244277f41789\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_35db244277f41789/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Conflicting guidance source of truth\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_4339357fd56b8213e42628c8\", \"member_5a27787407347c8ea5eb9259\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that a guide example contradicts the previous Friday’s alignment and asks whether a later announcement replaces an older note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"The same QA tutor asks in a separate thread whether to follow a pinned update or an older scoring-guide screenshot.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A different QA tutor answers the screenshot question by saying to follow the clarification in that thread for that case while the conflicting written examples are reconciled, and not to treat the older screenshot as independent authority. Verbatim quote: \\\"For this case, follow the clarification stated in this thread while the conflicting written examples are reconciled. Do not treat the older screenshot as independent authority.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ and instruction excerpts retrieved for this run address scoring dimensions and case-specific comparisons, but do not identify the disputed sources or establish whether one replaces another.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The QA tutor’s question about whether the later announcement replaces the older note remains unanswered in the earlier thread’s supplied messages.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval and follow-up records concern a batch-14 tie-calibration exercise and its sampled outcomes; neither establishes a decision about the reported source conflict or a standing source-precedence rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks in two threads which source to follow when written guidance appears to conflict.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A different QA tutor answered the screenshot question for that case, but the separate question about whether a later announcement replaces an older note remains unanswered in its thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\", \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the earlier thread, a QA tutor reports that a guide example contradicts the previous Friday’s alignment and asks whether a later announcement replaces an older note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the later thread, a different QA tutor says to follow the thread clarification for that case while the written examples are reconciled, rather than treating the older screenshot as independent authority.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current guidance retrieved for this run does not identify the disputed sources or settle whether one replaces another.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The earlier decision records retrieved for this run concern a batch-14 tie-calibration exercise, not the reported source conflict.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Arrange a focused comparison of the disputed sources with the QA tutor before settling the unanswered source-of-truth question. Draft to copy: Please join a focused review of the source conflict you raised in the earlier thread. Bring links and exact excerpts for the guide example, the previous Friday’s alignment, the later announcement and the older note, including their dates and scope. We will compare those records to determine whether the announcement replaces the note. The separate screenshot question received a case-specific answer from a QA tutor; that answer does not by itself settle the earlier question or establish a project-wide precedence rule. Scope: Limit the review to the unanswered announcement-versus-note question; do not assume the two threads concern identical sources.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The earlier supersession question remains unanswered, while the later thread has a case-specific answer. Comparing the actual records avoids extending that answer into an unsupported project-wide rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-approval@1.0:99b5da48\", \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): A QA tutor’s reported conflict between a guide example and an earlier alignment still lacks an answer about which source governs.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_4339357fd56b8213e42628c8\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_4339357fd56b8213e42628c8 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks whether a later announcement replaces an older note; the supplied thread contains no answer.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_5a27787407347c8ea5eb9259\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_5a27787407347c8ea5eb9259 is RESOLVED_IN_THREAD: A different QA tutor answers the question with case-specific handling: follow the thread clarification and do not treat the older screenshot as independent authority. This is an answer within the thread, not established project guidance.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"open_question\", \"kind\": \"OPEN_QUESTION\", \"text\": \"The cited evidence leaves this specific question unsettled: Does the later announcement replace the older note for the guide example raised in the earlier thread?\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: A QA tutor reports conflicting guidance and asks which scoring source to follow, indicating a contained risk of inconsistent handling. The messages do not establish batch-wide disruption or multiple distinct affected reporters.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[1]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Conflicting interpretations that affect, or are reasonably likely to affect, how tasks are scored or handled\\\": A QA tutor reports that a guide example contradicts an alignment and separately asks whether a pinned update or an older scoring-guide screenshot should govern.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U008\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U008 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:focused_source_review\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Schedule a short review session. Instruction: Arrange a focused comparison of the disputed sources with the QA tutor before settling the unanswered source-of-truth question. Draft to copy: Please join a focused review of the source conflict you raised in the earlier thread. Bring links and exact excerpts for the guide example, the previous Friday’s alignment, the later announcement and the older note, including their dates and scope. We will compare those records to determine whether the announcement replaces the note. The separate screenshot question received a case-specific answer from a QA tutor; that answer does not by itself settle the earlier question or establish a project-wide precedence rule. Why this helps: The earlier supersession question remains unanswered, while the later thread has a case-specific answer. Comparing the actual records avoids extending that answer into an unsupported project-wide rule. Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): A QA tutor’s reported conflict between a guide example and an earlier alignment still lacks an answer about which source governs.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:written_source_collection\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Reply in the unanswered thread asking the QA tutor for the disputed source links, exact excerpts, dates and scope for a written comparison before deciding whether a discussion is needed. Draft to copy: Please add links and exact excerpts for the guide example, the previous Friday’s alignment, the later announcement and the older note, including their dates and scope. I will compare them here and identify whether a source-of-truth decision still needs confirmation. The answer in the separate screenshot thread was limited to that case; I am not treating it as an answer to this question or as a project-wide rule. Why this helps: A written request gathers the missing records without requiring a meeting or choosing a governing source prematurely. It leaves a visible path to confirmation if comparing the records does not settle the question. Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): The supplied earlier thread contains a current question about conflicting sources but no answer, so a targeted request for the actual records is warranted now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:observe_without_new_intervention\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"No action needed now. Instruction: Leave the existing threads unchanged for now and watch for an answer to the earlier source-of-truth question without treating the separate case-specific reply as resolving it. Draft to copy: No new message for now. Watch for a reply to the earlier source-of-truth question and keep it open unless the disputed records establish an answer. Why this helps: Observation avoids duplicating a recent exchange from one reporting tutor, and the separate screenshot question already has a case-specific answer. However, waiting does not advance the unanswered supersession question, and no supplied message shows that someone has taken responsibility for it.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_GENERAL:1790874467.000044\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4339357fd56b8213e42628c8\", \"thread_id\": \"1790874467.000044\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:07:47.000044Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The guide example contradicts last Friday’s alignment. Can we check whether the later announcement replaces the older note?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790915967.000043\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_5a27787407347c8ea5eb9259\", \"thread_id\": \"1790915967.000043\", \"author_id\": \"U008\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:39:27.000043Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Should we follow the pinned update or the older scoring guide screenshot?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_RP_QA:1790916012.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_5a27787407347c8ea5eb9259\", \"thread_id\": \"1790915967.000043\", \"author_id\": \"U014\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T04:40:12.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U008\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"this\", \"users\": [\"U001\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"For this case, follow the clarification stated in this thread while the conflicting written examples are reconciled. Do not treat the older screenshot as independent authority.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790871613.000001:430efd10\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790871613.000001\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790871613.000001\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"upstream_review\": {\"review_required\": true, \"review_reasons\": [\"It is correct that no scoring method is supplied, but Avery does provide an example of misleading citation support: the source exists while its quoted paragraph addresses another claim. The rationale incorrectly says no examples were provided.\"]}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-01T16:20:13.000001+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_15): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nBatch status note — How to score responses with weak, missing, or misleading citations. Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\\n\\nContext reply [1790871661.000113] by U010 (TUTOR):\\nThe source is real, but the quoted paragraph is about a different claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:fa9b6a3d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction following\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction following\\n\\n### Q: The prompt required JSON, but one response is well-written prose. Which response wins?\\nThe required format is not optional: record its violation separately from factual accuracy. No universal tie-break rule is established for competing accuracy and instruction-following defects. If the actual pair and applicable guidance do not settle the preference, provide the prompt and both responses for TL confirmation.\\n\\n### Q: Can accuracy outweigh ignoring a requested output structure?\\nScore the dimensions separately and identify whether the requested structure was mandatory. Do not infer a general priority rule from one example or decide without the other response's evidence.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790929075.000039:05d4b538\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-02T08:17:55.000039+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790929075.000039\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790929075.000039\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-02T08:17:55.000039+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-02T08:17:55.000039+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-02T08:17:55.000039+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_15): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nBatch status note — QA and tutors disagree on when two outputs are tied. Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790936513.000019:8237860f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790936513.000019\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790936513.000019\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"MESSAGE_AUTHOR\", \"approval_status\": \"UNKNOWN\"}, \"authorship\": {\"author_id\": \"U001\", \"verified\": true, \"basis\": \"SLACK_MESSAGE_AUTHOR\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[ANNOUNCEMENT posted 2026-10-02T10:21:53.000019+00:00 by TEAM_LEAD (rp_batch_15): not established as handling for this topic until you show it is relevant and gives a directive.]\\nBatch status note — Competing rubric dimensions: factuality versus instruction adherence. Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\\n\\nContext reply [1790936562.000113] by U007 (QA_TUTOR):\\nWas the requested structure mandatory, and were the factual statements correct independently?\\n\\nContext reply [1790936607.000226] by U001 (TEAM_LEAD):\\nPlease paste the exact formatting instruction; QA needs to verify whether it was mandatory before weighing the responses.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:a71c54c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor describe task-quality defects and do not determine operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Factual accuracy | Error changes the central conclusion or actionable answer | Nonessential background error without that effect | Accurate paraphrase or an immaterial stylistic difference |\\n| Instruction adherence | Explicit required format/structure is missing | Limited violation of an actual secondary requirement | A stylistic choice that violates no requirement |\\n| Citation support | Fabricated reference or materially unsupported attribution | A limited citation-detail error where the source and support remain identifiable | A valid source that supports the claim |\\n| Preference | Identify a meaningful benefit; grade underlying defects separately | Do not manufacture a defect to break a tie | No meaningful quality difference supports a tie |\\n\\nAn inaccessible link needs a verification note; lack of access alone does not establish the error grade of the claim.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:47ed0c14\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Instruction adherence versus accuracy\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Instruction adherence versus accuracy\\nScore these dimensions separately. An explicit required output structure, such as JSON, is not optional.\\n\\nThis guidance does not define a universal preference ordering for a response that is stronger on accuracy but weaker on a required format. When the applicable rules and actual pair do not settle the comparison, provide the exact prompt, both responses and their separate defects for a TL decision. Do not assume facts about the other response.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-instructions@1.1:3350bbc0\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-instructions@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — Instructions (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors and citations\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-08-30T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors and citations\\n- A factual error is major when it changes the central conclusion or the answer a user would act on.\\n- A nonessential background error with no effect on that conclusion is minor.\\n- A broken link is an access/verification failure, not proof that the underlying factual claim is false.\\n- Distinguish an existing source that does not support the claim from an invented reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:response-preference-faq@1.1:3db12f63\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"response-preference-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Response Preference — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Factual errors\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"response-preference-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-05T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Factual errors\\n\\n### Q: What counts as a significant factual error?\\nAn error that changes the central conclusion or the answer the user would act on. A nonessential background detail with no effect on the recommendation is minor.\\n\\n### Q: The source link is dead. Should I penalize the factual claim?\\nRecord that the citation could not be verified. A failed URL alone does not prove the claim is false. Distinguish access failure from an unsupported attribution or fabricated reference.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790888971.000030:7db831c7\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT\", \"citation\": {\"title\": \"Slack announcement in response-preference-announcements at 2026-10-01T21:09:31.000030+00:00\", \"source\": {\"channel_id\": \"C_RP_ANNOUNCEMENTS\", \"message_id\": \"1790888971.000030\", \"system\": \"slack\", \"thread_id\": \"1790888971.000030\"}}, \"source_type\": \"announcement\", \"record_kind\": \"announcement\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-10-01T21:09:31.000030+00:00\", \"basis\": \"created_at\", \"created_at\": \"2026-10-01T21:09:31.000030+00:00\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"response_preference\", \"batch_id\": \"rp_batch_15\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"a