tus\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"pending_post\", \"outcome_status\": \"not_observed\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: pending_post; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# RP-20260916-01 — Approve tie calibration advice\\n\\n## Context\\nThe prior batch's calibration packet contained one pair differing only in wording and another in which one response omitted a fact needed for the user's request. Reviewers were using “slightly clearer” without explaining whether it changed usefulness.\\n\\n## Suggested advice\\nThe simulated Advisor proposed a brief alignment announcement and a review of eight sampled pairs, using the existing meaningful-quality-difference criterion.\\n\\n## TL approval\\nAlex approved the proposal. Ask reviewers to identify the actual user-facing benefit; a cosmetic wording preference alone is not sufficient. Keep material accuracy or instruction defects visible rather than forcing ties.\\n\\nThis is a calibration of the existing criterion, not a new numerical preference threshold. The approval covers the batch-14 exercise.\\n\\n## State\\nPosting and the review exercise are authorized but not recorded as completed in this approval.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0:f678161f\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome@1.0\", \"title\": \"Tie calibration follow-up — improvement in the reviewed sample\", \"sections\": [\"Review receipt\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"rp-tie-calibration-outcome\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"follow_up\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"history\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"d